 "signs": [
  {
   "x": 21,
   "y": 9,
   "text": "FERRY TERMINAL. Sail from the Mersey to the Isle of Man. Bring a sandwich. And a sailor's hat if you've got one."
  },
  {
   "x": 18,
   "y": 9,
   "text": "FERRY TO DOUGLAS. Departures when the tide, the captain and the seagulls agree."
  },
  {
   "x": 33,
   "y": 18,
   "text": "THE FAB FOUR, in bronze. Please do not ask them to get back together. They've heard."
  },
  {
   "x": 18,
   "y": 18,
   "text": "SUPERLAMBANANA. It's exactly what it says. A banana-lamb. Don't think too hard."
  },
  {
   "x": 30,
   "y": 15,
   "text": "THE LIVER BIRDS. If they fly away, Liverpool ceases to exist. They have a very good union."
  },
  {
   "x": 46,
   "y": 20,
   "text": "ALBERT DOCK, 1846. The first warehouses built with no wood at all. Only brick, iron and stone. The fire brigade were overjoyed."
  },
  {
   "x": 33,
   "y": 29,
   "text": "THE CAVERN (ISH). Where four lads once played 292 times. Our drummer plays only 291. Keeper's Club. Members only. And you."
  },
  {
   "x": 16,
   "y": 35,
   "text": "LIME STREET. Beautiful station. Terrible at timetables. Excellent at goodbyes."
  },
  {
   "x": 47,
   "y": 38,
   "text": "LIVERPOOL CATHEDRAL. Biggest in Britain. Took 74 years to finish. Builders apparently on a tea break."
  },
  {
   "x": 41,
   "y": 42,
   "text": "SEFTON PARK-ISH. Dunes, ducks and a man throwing a ball for a very tired dog."
  },
  {
   "x": 60,
   "y": 23,
   "text": "EAST: Chat Moss and Manchester. Scouse to Manc: 'You're a long way from the sea'."
  },
  {
   "x": 29,
   "y": 54,
   "text": "SOUTH: the Wirral Way and Chester. Mind the tide."
  }
 ],
